## iframes

Unlike Selenium, Playwright doesn't require switching context. `frameLocator()` scopes queries directly:

```ts
const frame = page.frameLocator('#payment-iframe');
await frame.getByLabel('Card number').fill('4242 4242 4242 4242');
```

## Shadow DOM

Playwright's locators **pierce open shadow roots automatically** — `getByRole`, `getByText`, and CSS selectors all work transparently across shadow boundaries without any special syntax, which is a major advantage when testing apps built with web components (Lit, Stencil, etc.).

```ts
// Works even if <my-button> uses shadow DOM internally
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Checkout' }).click();
```

