## The Interaction API

```ts
await page.getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Search' }).fill('Playwright');
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Search' }).click();
await page.getByLabel('Country').selectOption('Pakistan');
await page.getByText('Draft').hover();
await page.locator('#drag-source').dragTo(page.locator('#drop-target'));
await page.getByLabel('Upload resume').setInputFiles('resume.pdf');
```

All of these are auto-waited and simulate real trusted browser events (not just DOM attribute mutations), so they trigger the same JS event listeners a real user interaction would — critical for testing React/Vue apps with complex event handling.

