## Downloads

```ts
const [download] = await Promise.all([
  page.waitForEvent('download'),
  page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Export CSV' }).click(),
]);
await download.saveAs('/tmp/export.csv');
```

## Uploads

```ts
await page.getByLabel('Upload avatar').setInputFiles('avatar.png');
```

Note the `Promise.all` pattern for downloads — you must register the listener **before** triggering the action that causes the event, otherwise the event can fire before you're listening for it.

lessons.starter_code:
import { test } from '@playwright/test';

test('confirm delete dialog and verify download', async ({ page }) => {
  page.on('dialog', dialog => dialog.accept());

  await page.goto('/reports');
  const [download] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Export CSV' }).click(),
  ]);
  await download.saveAs('/tmp/report.csv');
});

lessons.content_markdown:
## Why Page Objects Still Matter

Even with resilient locators, hardcoding selectors across dozens of test files creates massive duplication. The Page Object Model (POM) centralizes locators and actions per page/component.

```ts
// pages/LoginPage.ts
import { Page, Locator, expect } from '@playwright/test';

export class LoginPage {
  readonly page: Page;
  readonly email: Locator;
  readonly password: Locator;
  readonly submit: Locator;

  constructor(page: Page) {
    this.page = page;
    this.email = page.getByLabel('Email');
    this.password = page.getByLabel('Password');
    this.submit = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Log in' });
  }

  async goto() {
    await this.page.goto('/login');
  }

  async login(email: string, password: string) {
    await this.email.fill(email);
    await this.password.fill(password);
    await this.submit.click();
  }
}
```

Tests then read like plain English:
```ts
const loginPage = new LoginPage(page);
await loginPage.goto();
await loginPage.login('qa@zaka.dev', 'Secure123!');
await expect(page.getByText('Welcome back')).toBeVisible();
```

