lessons.content_markdown:
## Custom Fixtures

Instead of copy-pasting login logic into every test's `beforeEach`, Playwright lets you extend `test` with fixtures — dependency-injected, automatically cleaned up, and composable.

```ts
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test';
import { LoginPage } from './pages/LoginPage';

type Fixtures = { loginPage: LoginPage; authedPage: void };

export const test = base.extend<Fixtures>({
  loginPage: async ({ page }, use) => {
    await use(new LoginPage(page));
  },
  authedPage: async ({ page, loginPage }, use) => {
    await loginPage.goto();
    await loginPage.login('qa@zaka.dev', 'Secure123!');
    await use();
  },
});
```

Now any test can simply request `authedPage` as a parameter and start already logged in — no repeated boilerplate, and fixtures compose cleanly across many test files.

