## Beyond the Browser

Playwright ships a full HTTP client (`APIRequestContext`) that shares cookies/auth with the browser context — perfect for fast API tests or for **seeding state before a UI test** (e.g., creating a user via API instead of clicking through a signup form).

```ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('API: create and verify a course', async ({ request }) => {
  const res = await request.post('/api/courses', {
    data: { title: 'Appium Mastery', slug: 'appium-mastery' },
  });
  expect(res.ok()).toBeTruthy();

  const body = await res.json();
  expect(body.slug).toBe('appium-mastery');
});
```

This hybrid approach — API for setup, UI for the actual behavior under test — is one of the biggest speed wins in modern test suites.

